            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Cosmos DB Request Unit Throttling\n**WHAT:** Cosmos DB Request Unit Throttling: saturation signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `database-platform` (database / azure_cosmos_db, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** HTTP 429 from Cosmos is a hard provisioned-throughput boundary. Any throttling is real customer latency.\n\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/cosmos-ru-throttling.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-scale-workload` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `database-capacity.stage.database-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-database-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Cosmos DB Request Unit Throttling — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/cosmos-ru-throttling.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Cosmos DB Request Unit Throttling — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/cosmos-ru-throttling.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Cosmos DB Request Unit Throttling\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-database-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
