            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Datadog Agent Unhealthy\n**WHAT:** Datadog Agent Unhealthy: telemetry_health signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (infrastructure / host, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Agent presence is binary and is the precondition for every other host signal — this is the monitor that protects the monitoring.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-agent-unhealthy.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-host` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `compute.stage.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Datadog Agent Unhealthy — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-agent-unhealthy.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Datadog Agent Unhealthy — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-agent-unhealthy.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Data