            "id": "314372380",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Disk Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHAT:** Replaces \"disk \u003e 90%\". A volume steady at 92% for two years is not an incident; a volume at 60% growing 8%/day is. Three days of lead time is the shortest window in which a human can reliably act.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `compute-platform` (infrastructure / host, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-disk-exhaustion-forecast.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `storage.stage.compute-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-infra-compute-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Disk Exhaustion Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-disk-exhaustion-forecast.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Disk Exhaustion Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/host-disk-exhaustion-forecast.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Disk Exhaustion Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-infra-compute-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.95",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.9",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
